The primitive-recursion body is the approximable map sending a function k and a pair of arguments x and y to the conditional of the zero test of x, the value f at y, and g at the predecessor of x, at y, and at k applied to that predecessor and y. It is the conditional composed with the pairing of that zero test, f at the second argument, and g at the predecessor of the first argument, the second argument, and the evaluation of k there.
